0..77 Comment "// Two rules of one operation that overlap at `pick(Zero, n)` and leave it at"
78..148 Comment "// `plus(Zero, n)` and at `plus(n, Zero)`, one call with its arguments"
149..227 Comment "// swapped. Neither normal form is a value, so completion would join them by a"
228..305 Comment "// rule, and the path order orients a rule between a call and its permutation"
306..351 Comment "// neither way: the block is refused by name."
352..354 Comment "//"
355..369 Comment "// - see: #338"
371..446 Comment "/// An operation whose two overlapping rules swap the arguments of the call"
447..462 Comment "/// they leave."
